From bb5d1772907db0568ed3966b6ebd6fb0ff6a85f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lyqed <antondoeswonders@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 15:52:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] localratelimit: support a custom rate limit exceeded response

Adds an optional `response` field to the local rate limit policy so
operators can customize the body, content type, and status code returned
when a limit is exceeded, mirroring how the remote rate limiter already
returns the rate limit service's raw_body on rejection.

The X-RateLimit-* headers are still attached, and gRPC requests keep the
trailers-only grpc-status response. When `response` is unset the
existing plain-text 429 behavior is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Lyqed <antondoeswonders@gmail.com>
